if {convo_progress.gawain.tutorialSeen} == false:
	jump gawainTutorial/
gawain: Oh, Percy! Can I help you with anything?
label discussionTree
- (Let's chat.)
	gawain: Aw, you wanna spend time with little ol' me? Anything you're curious about?
	- (How are you?)
		gawain: Me? I'm alright, I think. I lived a full life outside, pretty much, so I'm not consumed with angst like everyone else here.
	- (What's with this place?)
		gawain: I think you remember Camlann? There used to be a church here, but at some point it turned into a hotel to suit this changed world. Fine by me, I say. It was pretty stuffy as a church, and now I've got a computer here. It's got pinball on it! Wanna play?
		- (Not right now.)
			Right, sure. Yeah, you're busy, aren't you?
		- (Sure.)
			Viktor: Hey Nina how do you feel about a pinball minigame
	- (About the others...)
		gawain: Oo, it's gossip you're after? Ask and ye shall recieve, friend.
		- (Merlin)
			gawain: He's still a grouch, nothing new there. He's set himself up by the stairwell going down, making sure no one goes down there. Says it's something dangerous. Poppycock to that, but it's not like I know what's really down there.
			gawain: No, wait, I guess I kinda know what's down there. The water from the atrium goes underground, so maybe those stairs go to where it drains.
			gawain: That's all I got, though.
		- (Arthur)
			gawain: You have to promise me you won't snitch to his highness about whatever I say, alright? It's not like he can fire me or anything, but he's still the boss.
			Your secrets are safe with me, Gawain.
			gawain: Knew I could <trust you/count on you>, Percy.
- (I need to review something.)
	gawain: Hit your head, Percy? Joking, joking. What do you need a refresher on?
	label reviewTree
	- Notes
		gawain: You should really be writing things down in that little notebooks of yours. Folks will understand you're here on a quest, so it won't seem odd for you to open it up and glance at it during a conversation. You should jot things down too, but not too much. Three words at a time is a good limit; don't wanna write down everything someone says. <They'd probably think it's rude./You'd probably hurt your hand doing that.>
		gawain: 'Course, once you're done talking with someone, you can take out that book of yours and jot down whatever you want. Might be a bit difficult to get someone's exact wording after the fact, though, so don't expect to play catch up after the fact.
	- Possessions and Feelings
		gawain: It's a good idea to make to note of what belongs to who. That goes for feelings, too.
	gawain: You got everything figured out, now?
	- (Yes.)
	- (No.)
		jump reviewTree
- (I'm a bit lost.)
	if {questProgress.sequenceRepair.sequenceStatus} == "broken":
		if {convo_progress.bedivere.bedivereGreeted} == false:
			gawain: Sequence still looks broken. You talked to Bedivere about fixing it yet? I haven't seen him around here, so I bet he's still working on whatever went wrong in the executive suites. That's on the top floor.
		else:
			Can you tell me what Bedivere was working on?
			gawain: Huh? Sure, I'll check my little logbook. Well, I say book. It's all on the computer now. Saves paper, apparently, but our paper just sorta... appears so I'm not sure if it even comes from anywhere. Anyway, looks like he was called up for [insert problem here.]
	if {convo_progress.merlin.merlinGreeted} == false:
		gawain: Have you talked to Merlin yet? He's good with all that magic stuff. Maybe he's got some idea what that kingfisher of yours means.
gawain: So, that everything, Percy, or do you got something else on your mind?
- (That's it, thanks.)
	gawain: See you around, then!
- (Something else.)
	gawain: Well then, let's hear it!
	jump discussionTree